1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:02,040
If you lay flat boards across the top of

2
00:00:02,060 --> 00:00:03,180
your walls, you have a roof.

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:05,120
But the rain sits on it in puddles and

4
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:06,220
drips through every gap.

5
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:08,440
So you tilt it and the water runs off.

6
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:10,480
But it still finds the cracks between the

7
00:00:10,540 --> 00:00:10,880
boards.

8
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:13,180
So you cover them with small flat pieces,

9
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:15,180
each row lapped over the one below, like

10
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:16,160
the scales of a fish.

11
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,320
These are shingles.

12
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:19,520
But a strong wind drives the rain up

13
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:20,240
underneath them.

14
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:22,120
So you roll out a waterproof sheet below.

15
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:23,440
This is underlayment.

16
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:25,940
But now all that water pours off the edge

17
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,380
and digs a trench along your walls.

18
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:29,520
So you hang a trough under the edge and

19
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:30,500
run a pipe down the corner.

20
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:32,540
This is a gutter, and it carries the rain

21
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:33,560
away from your house.

22
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:35,860
But the first big snow weighs as much as

23
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:36,820
six cars.

24
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:39,040
The roof sags and pushes your walls apart.

25
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:40,780
So you tie the bottom of every pair of

26
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:42,560
rafters together into a triangle.

27
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:43,620
This is a truss.

28
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:45,500
But the warm air from your house heats the

29
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:46,140
roof from below.

30
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:48,380
The snow melts, runs down to the cold

31
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:50,500
edge, and freezes into a wall of ice that

32
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:52,380
pushes water back up under your shingles.

33
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:53,560
This is an ice dam.

34
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:55,600
So you lay a blanket of insulation on the

35
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,500
attic floor and let cold air flow through

36
00:00:57,520 --> 00:00:57,840
above it.

37
00:00:58,080 --> 00:00:59,840
And those pretty icicles are not a sign of

38
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:00,100
winter.

39
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,880
They are a sign your house is leaking

40
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:02,200
heat.

41
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:03,920
Add a strip of metal around the chimney.

42
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:06,760
Congratulations, you have built a roof.
